Start at the boundary: no command parser sees bytes until
`rk_secure_open_request()` succeeds.

Keep one secure channel inside the agent.
Start it before the worker and stop it after the worker joins.
The frame remains transport; the secure envelope is its payload.

For `SHELL port`, parse into a temporary command, require the action gate, and
delegate only admission to `rk_root_shell_request()`.
The imported component owns the shell lifetime.

On unload, close and join the control agent first.
Then stop the root shell.
